    <comment>NEW PACKAGE (supersedes sr#1372084): Suggests python-tree-sitter &gt;= 0.22 instead of Requires, matching tree-sitter-bash, so ring1/product installcheck does not demand a non-ring package.

- Convert the Python binding to the shared loader pattern
  (%treesitter_python_install only, singlespec
  python_subpackage_only): generate a _binding.py that loads
  the grammar library this package ships instead of compiling
  the upstream C extension. Drop the C-extension Python
  BuildRequires (devel/pip/setuptools/wheel).
- The python subpackage now Requires %{name} =
  %{version}-%{release}.
- Suggests python-tree-sitter &gt;= 0.22 instead of Requires,
  matching tree-sitter-bash, so ring1/product installcheck
  does not demand a non-ring package.
- Run a functional %check parsing Scala source through the
  shim; gated to suse_version &gt;= 1699 because
  python-tree-sitter does not exist in Leap 16.0.

INTERDEPENDENT REQUESTS - please stage together:
 * sr#1372054 - tree-sitter (python binding macros)
 * sibling new-grammar SRs from editors:tree-sitter
Needed for python-graphifyy.</comment>
